  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Village playing of the krylovidnye (wing-shaped) gusli, a plucked psaltery held on the knees, which survived into the 20th century in the Pskov and Novgorod regions of north-western Russia, where players strummed across the strings while the fingers of the other hand damped those not wanted, to accompany dances and chastushki. Soviet folklorists recorded the last village players in the Pskov region, and their style became a basis of the modern gusli revival.",
